The T5 code encoder implements the T5 v1.1 encoder architecture (Raffel et al.,
2020, https://github.com/google-research/text-to-text-transfer-transformer).
The released T5 weights are fine-tuned from google/t5-v1_1-small
(https://huggingface.co/google/t5-v1_1-small), and the tokenizer.json shipped
with them is converted from that model's SentencePiece vocabulary. Both are
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (attribution: Google); the
license text is included in licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.

The training objective follows SLAP (Guinot et al., 2025). The projector and
predictor heads here are an independent implementation; no SLAP source code is
included.

