FAUST EFFECT SOURCES (src/peace/dsp)

The effects import the Faust standard libraries (https://github.com/grame-cncm/
faustlibraries, GRAME), which are not included. Files adapted from those
libraries or from other projects keep their original terms:

- compressor.dsp: a Faust port of the compressor in the Vital synthesizer
  (https://github.com/mtytel/vital), Copyright 2013-2019 Matt Tytel, licensed
  under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later. The license text is
  in licenses/GPL-3.0.txt.
- reverb_spring.dsp: adapted from re.springreverb by Daniel Leonov in the Faust
  libraries (reverbs.lib), whose demo declares the MIT license.
- flanger.dsp and phaser.dsp: adapted from the flanger and phaser demos by
  Julius O. Smith III in the Faust libraries (demos.lib, GRAME, LGPL).
- reverb_freeverb.dsp: adapted from freeverb_demo by Romain Michon in the Faust
  libraries.
- reverb_zita.dsp: adapted from zita_rev1 by Julius O. Smith III in the Faust
  libraries.
- klonCentaur.dsp, reverb_dattorro.dsp, and reverb_vital.dsp call library
  functions (ve.klonCentaur, a BSD 3-Clause port of Chowdhury-DSP's ChowCentaur;
  re.dattorro_rev; re.vital_rev) and contain no code from them.

The remaining effect sources are original to this project and MIT-licensed.
